  "body": "<p>A PR agency in Chicago helps you get your business into the publications that Chicagoans and the city's business community read. That means finding the story in what you already do, writing it to fit a particular title and placing it so it keeps working for you whenever someone searches your name.</p><p>We work with Chicago businesses remotely and handle the process from start to finish. We develop the story with you, write it to the publication's standard, manage the placement, and you approve every word before it goes live. You come away with coverage you can share with clients, include in proposals and use to show partners that your business is established.</p><h2 id=\"who-pr-in-chicago-suits\">Who PR in Chicago suits</h2><p>Chicago has a strong culture of trust and relationships in business, and a credible piece of coverage helps open doors. PR in Chicago tends to suit:</p><ul><li>Trading, fintech and financial services firms in the Loop and beyond</li><li>Logistics, distribution and manufacturing companies that serve the wider Midwest</li><li>Restaurants, bars and food brands in a city famous for its dining</li><li>Consulting, legal and professional firms that sell on reputation</li><li>Founders and startups who want investors and hires to take them seriously</li></ul><h2 id=\"the-chicago-media-landscape\">The Chicago media landscape</h2><p>The <strong>Chicago Tribune</strong> is the city's best-known newspaper and one of the most established mastheads in the Midwest. A story in the Tribune is something Chicago clients recognise straight away, and it remains a reference point for news across Illinois.</p><p>For business readers, <strong>Business Journal Chicago</strong> covers deals, growth and leadership across the region, and the <strong>Chicago Journal</strong> follows local news and the people behind it. The right choice depends on who you want to reach: a story about a new restaurant in Wicker Park and a story about a logistics firm expanding near O'Hare belong in different places, and we match each story to the title whose readers are most likely to act on it.</p><h2 id=\"what-stories-travel-in-chicago\">What stories travel in Chicago</h2><p>Chicago's economy is broad. It is a centre of finance and futures trading, a national hub for rail, road and air freight, and home to manufacturing, food production, consulting and healthcare. Its restaurant scene, architecture and neighbourhoods give lifestyle stories a strong local hook as well.</p><p>Stories that travel in Chicago tend to be grounded and practical: a business growing jobs in the city, a founder bringing a new idea to an established industry, or a company solving a problem Midwestern customers recognise. Chicago readers respond to substance over hype, so we focus on the detail that shows what your business actually does and why it matters here.</p><h2 id=\"local-state-and-national-coverage-together\">Local, state and national coverage together</h2><p>Chicago businesses often serve customers well beyond the city limits. A Chicago title builds local trust, while papers across Illinois, such as the <strong>Rockford Register Star</strong>, <strong>The State Journal-Register</strong> in Springfield and the <strong>Journal Star</strong> in Peoria, reach customers downstate. We plan placements together, so a single story can give you a Chicago presence and reach readers elsewhere in Illinois at the same time.</p><h2 id=\"how-it-works-with-dna\">How it works with DNA</h2><ul><li><strong>Story:</strong> we talk through your business and find the Chicago angle worth publishing.</li><li><strong>Writing:</strong> we draft the piece to the standard and style of the chosen title.</li><li><strong>Approval:</strong> you review and approve every word before it goes live.</li><li><strong>Placement:</strong> we manage the placement and send you the live article.</li></ul><p>Most placements take weeks rather than days, depending on the title and how quickly drafts are approved.</p><h2 id=\"publications-we-place-in-chicago\">Publications we place in for Chicago</h2>\n<p>These are the Chicago titles we place clients in. Where a title has its own page, it explains what it publishes and how a feature there works.</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/get-featured-in/chicago-tribune\">Chicago Tribune</a></li><li><strong>Business Journal Chicago</strong></li><li><a href=\"/get-featured-in/chicago-journal\">Chicago Journal</a></li></ul>\n<h3>Across Illinois</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>Journal Star</strong></li><li><strong>The State Journal-Register</strong></li><li><strong>Belleville News-Democrat</strong></li><li><strong>Quad-City Times</strong></li><li><strong>Rockford Register Star</strong></li><li><strong>The Pantagraph</strong></li><li><strong>Moline Dispatch &amp; Rock Island Argus</strong></li><li><strong>Freeport Journal Standard</strong></li><li><strong>Galesburg Register Mail</strong></li><li><strong>Anglotopia</strong></li><li><strong>Herald &amp; Review</strong></li><li><strong>Journal Gazette &amp; Times-Courier</strong></li><li><strong>Canton Daily Ledger</strong></li><li><strong>McDonough County Voice</strong></li><li><strong>Pekin Daily Times</strong></li></ul>\n<p>See every title we place in across the state on our <a href=\"/pr-in/illinois\">PR agency in Illinois</a> page.</p>\n<h2 id=\"frequently-asked-questions\">Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Do I need a local PR agency in Chicago?</h3><p>No. What matters is knowing Chicago's titles and writing to their standard. We work with businesses in Chicago remotely, and the finished coverage reads the same to your clients.</p><h3>How do I get featured in Chicago newspapers?</h3><p>Start with a story tied to the city and a title whose readers match your customers. We help you shape that story, write it for the publication and manage the placement, with your approval throughout.</p><h3>What does a Chicago PR agency do?</h3><p>A Chicago PR agency finds the angle in your business, writes it for the right local titles and handles the placement, so you get coverage that builds trust with clients and partners across the city.</p>",
  "toc": [{"id": "who-pr-in-chicago-suits", "text": "Who PR in Chicago suits"}, {"id": "the-chicago-media-landscape", "text": "The Chicago media landscape"}, {"id": "what-stories-travel-in-chicago", "text": "What stories travel in Chicago"}, {"id": "local-state-and-national-coverage-together", "text": "Local, state and national coverage together"}, {"id": "how-it-works-with-dna", "text": "How it works with DNA"}, {"id": "publications-we-place-in-chicago", "text": "Publications we place in for Chicago"}, {"id": "frequently-asked-questions", "text": "Frequently asked questions"}],
  "takeaways": ["Chicago coverage lands best when it ties to the city's real strengths, from finance and freight to food and manufacturing.", "The Chicago Tribune and Business Journal Chicago reach different readers, so matching the story to the title matters.", "We develop the story, write it to the publication's standard and manage the placement, and you approve every word."],
