  "intro": "Houston is a city of builders, from energy and engineering to food and healthcare, and its business community pays attention to who is getting covered. We work with businesses in Houston to turn their work into stories that local readers and clients can find.",
  "outlets": ["fort-worth-star-telegram"],
  "body": "<p>A PR agency in Houston helps you get your business in front of the people who read Houston media, from customers in the suburbs to decision-makers in the Energy Corridor. The work comes down to finding the story in what you already do, writing it for a specific title and placing it where it will keep appearing when someone searches for you.</p><p>We work with Houston businesses remotely and manage the whole process. We develop the story with you, write it to the publication's standard, manage the placement, and you approve every word before it goes live. You get coverage you can send to prospects, add to bids and proposals, and use to show new contacts that your business is established.</p><h2 id=\"who-pr-in-houston-suits\">Who PR in Houston suits</h2><p>Houston is large, spread out and entrepreneurial, and a piece of coverage helps a business stand out across a very wide metro. PR in Houston tends to suit:</p><ul><li>Energy, engineering and industrial services firms, including those moving into cleaner energy</li><li>Healthcare providers, clinics and life sciences companies</li><li>Restaurants and food brands in one of the most varied dining cities in the country</li><li>Property developers, builders and home services firms across a growing region</li><li>Founders and small businesses in Montrose, the Heights and the suburbs looking for local credibility</li></ul><h2 id=\"the-houston-media-landscape\">The Houston media landscape</h2><p>Houston has a mix of business titles, local news and long-running alternative weeklies. <strong>Business Journal Houston</strong> reaches owners and executives across the region and is a natural home for stories about growth, deals and leadership. The <strong>Houston Press</strong> is known for its coverage of food, arts, music and city life, and suits restaurants, venues and consumer brands with a strong local identity.</p><p>The <strong>Houston Times</strong> covers local news and the people behind Houston businesses. Because each title has its own readers, a story about a new Vietnamese restaurant in Bellaire and a story about an engineering firm winning work along the Ship Channel need different homes, and choosing the right one is part of what we do.</p><h2 id=\"what-stories-travel-in-houston\">What stories travel in Houston</h2><p>Houston is known around the world for oil and gas, and energy still shapes much of its economy, alongside petrochemicals, the port and the Ship Channel, a vast medical district and NASA's human spaceflight operations nearby. The city is also one of the most diverse in the country, and its food scene reflects that.</p><p>Stories that travel in Houston are often about practical progress: a company creating jobs, an energy business adapting to change, a clinic serving a growing neighbourhood or a family restaurant that has become a local institution. Houston readers respect people who build things, so we focus on what your business has actually done and why it matters to the city.</p><h2 id=\"local-state-and-national-coverage-together\">Local, state and national coverage together</h2><p>Many Houston businesses work across Texas and beyond. A Houston title builds trust close to home, the <strong>Fort Bend Star</strong> reaches the fast-growing suburbs to the southwest, and papers such as the <strong>Fort Worth Star-Telegram</strong> carry a story to readers in North Texas. We plan placements together, so one strong story can give you a Houston presence and statewide reach at the same time.</p><h2 id=\"how-it-works-with-dna\">How it works with DNA</h2><ul><li><strong>Story:</strong> we talk through your business and find the Houston angle worth publishing.</li><li><strong>Writing:</strong> we draft the piece to the style and standard of the chosen title.</li><li><strong>Approval:</strong> you review and approve every word before it goes live.</li><li><strong>Placement:</strong> we manage the placement and send you the live article.</li></ul><p>Most placements take weeks rather than days, depending on the title and how quickly drafts are signed off.</p><h2 id=\"publications-we-place-in-houston\">Publications we place in for Houston</h2>\n<p>These are the Houston titles we place clients in. Where a title has its own page, it explains what it publishes and how a feature there works.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Business Journal Houston</strong></li><li><strong>Houston Press</strong></li><li><strong>Houston Times</strong></li></ul>\n<h3>Across Texas</h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/get-featured-in/fort-worth-star-telegram\">Fort Worth Star-Telegram</a></li><li><strong>El Paso Times</strong></li><li><strong>Lubbock Avalanche-Journal</strong></li><li><strong>Wichita Falls Times-Record-News</strong></li><li><strong>Waco Tribune-Herald</strong></li><li><strong>GoSanAngelo</strong></li><li><strong>Abilene Reporter News</strong></li><li><strong>Caller Times</strong></li><li><strong>Amarillo Globe-News</strong></li><li><strong>KDAF</strong></li><li><strong>The Eagle</strong></li><li><strong>San Marcos Daily Record</strong></li><li><strong>My Aggie Nation</strong></li><li><strong>Fredericksburg Standard Radio-Post</strong></li><li><strong>Fort Bend Star</strong></li></ul>\n<p>See every title we place in across the state on our <a href=\"/pr-in/texas\">PR agency in Texas</a> page.</p>\n<h2 id=\"frequently-asked-questions\">Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Do I need a Houston-based PR firm to get local coverage?</h3><p>No. What matters is knowing which Houston titles reach your customers and writing to their standard. We work with Houston businesses remotely, and the coverage reads exactly the same.</p><h3>How do I get featured in Houston newspapers?</h3><p>Begin with a story that has a clear Houston angle, such as local jobs, a new location or a change in your industry. We shape it, write it for the right title and manage the placement, and you approve it before it runs.</p><h3>What does a Houston PR agency do?</h3><p>A Houston PR agency turns what your business does into stories for local and Texas titles and handles the placement, giving you coverage that builds trust with customers, partners and the city's business community.</p>",
  "toc": [{"id": "who-pr-in-houston-suits", "text": "Who PR in Houston suits"}, {"id": "the-houston-media-landscape", "text": "The Houston media landscape"}, {"id": "what-stories-travel-in-houston", "text": "What stories travel in Houston"}, {"id": "local-state-and-national-coverage-together", "text": "Local, state and national coverage together"}, {"id": "how-it-works-with-dna", "text": "How it works with DNA"}, {"id": "publications-we-place-in-houston", "text": "Publications we place in for Houston"}, {"id": "frequently-asked-questions", "text": "Frequently asked questions"}],
  "takeaways": ["Houston coverage works best when it ties to the city's real economy, from energy and the port to healthcare and food.", "Business Journal Houston and the Houston Press reach very different readers, so the title has to fit the story.", "We develop the story, write it to the publication's standard and manage the placement, and you approve every word."],
