  "intro": "We help Kansas City businesses get featured in the Kansas City Star and established publications across Missouri. We develop the story, write it to each title's standard and manage the placement, and you approve every word.",
  "outlets": ["kansas-city-star"],
  "body": "<p>A PR agency in Kansas City helps your business reach the people who matter on both sides of the state line: customers, suppliers, investors and the skilled people you want to hire. The goal is a credible, well-written article about your company in a publication Kansas City readers already trust, written as real news rather than a sales message.</p><p>Digital Networking Agency works with businesses in Kansas City remotely. We develop the story, write it to each publication's standard, manage the placement and send the draft to you, so you approve every word before it goes live. It gives a Kansas City company recognised Missouri coverage without building a press team of its own.</p><h2 id=\"who-pr-in-kansas-city-suits\">Who PR in Kansas City suits</h2><p>Kansas City has a varied economy, with strengths in engineering, logistics, animal health, financial services and a growing technology sector. The businesses that benefit most from coverage here include:</p><ul><li><strong>Engineering, architecture and construction firms</strong>, a field in which the Kansas City area has a strong reputation.</li><li><strong>Logistics, rail and distribution companies</strong> using the city's central location and transport links.</li><li><strong>Animal health and agricultural businesses</strong> connected to the wider region's farming economy.</li><li><strong>Health technology and software start-ups</strong> growing alongside established local employers.</li><li><strong>Restaurants, food producers and hospitality businesses</strong> in a city famous for its barbecue.</li></ul><h2 id=\"the-kansas-city-media-landscape\">The Kansas City media landscape</h2><p>The Kansas City Star is the city's long-established daily newspaper and the title most readers across the metro area associate with local news. It covers business, government, sport, food and community life on both the Missouri and Kansas sides of the city. A feature there gives a Kansas City business strong, shareable credibility with customers and partners throughout the region.</p><p>Beyond Kansas City, Missouri has a well-established set of regional titles. STL Today, the online home of the St. Louis Post-Dispatch, reaches readers on the other side of the state. The Springfield News Leader covers the south-west of Missouri and the Ozarks, and the Columbia Daily Tribune serves Columbia, home of the University of Missouri. For law firms and professional services, Missouri Lawyers speaks directly to the state's legal community.</p><h2 id=\"what-stories-travel-in-kansas-city\">What stories travel in Kansas City</h2><p>Kansas City readers respond to stories about practical growth, local character and the businesses building the city's future. Angles we develop regularly include:</p><ul><li>Engineering and infrastructure projects, from transport to energy and water.</li><li>Logistics and distribution growth, building on the city's central position in the country.</li><li>Animal health, agriculture and food science across the region.</li><li>Technology and start-up growth, including founders choosing Kansas City over the coasts.</li><li>Food, music and culture, including the city's barbecue and jazz traditions.</li></ul><p>A good story needs a reason to run now. We look for the timely element in your business, such as an expansion, new jobs, a contract, a product launch or a founder's informed view on the region's economy.</p><h2 id=\"local-state-and-national-coverage-together\">Local, state and national coverage together</h2><p>Many Kansas City businesses sell well beyond the metro area, so we plan coverage in layers. The Kansas City Star establishes you at home. Titles such as STL Today, the Springfield News Leader and the Columbia Daily Tribune extend your reach to other Missouri communities. National business coverage then adds weight when you are speaking to investors, partners and customers in other states.</p><h2 id=\"how-it-works-with-dna\">How it works with DNA</h2><p>We begin with a conversation about your business and what you want coverage to achieve in Kansas City and beyond. We then recommend the publications that fit, develop the angle and write the article in the style each title expects. You review the draft and approve every word. Once approved, we manage the placement through to publication and share the live coverage with you. The process takes weeks rather than days.</p><h2 id=\"publications-we-place-in-kansas-city\">Publications we place in for Kansas City</h2>\n<p>These are the Kansas City titles we place clients in. Where a title has its own page, it explains what it publishes and how a feature there works.</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/get-featured-in/kansas-city-star\">Kansas City Star</a></li></ul>\n<h3>Across Missouri</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>STL Today</strong></li><li><strong>Springfield News Leader</strong></li><li><strong>Columbia Daily Tribune</strong></li><li><strong>Missouri Lawyers</strong></li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"frequently-asked-questions\">Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Do I need a Kansas City PR agency to get local coverage?</h3><p>No. What matters is understanding Kansas City and Missouri media and writing to each publication's standard. We work with Kansas City businesses remotely and manage the whole process for you.</p><h3>How do I get featured in the Kansas City Star?</h3><p>Start with a timely story that matters to Kansas City readers, such as growth, new jobs, a product launch or community investment. We develop it, write it to the paper's standard and manage the placement, and you approve the final text.</p><h3>What does a PR agency in Kansas City do?</h3><p>It finds the newsworthy angle in your business, prepares articles for Kansas City and Missouri publications and handles each placement. With DNA, nothing goes live until you have approved every word.</p>",
  "toc": [{"id": "who-pr-in-kansas-city-suits", "text": "Who PR in Kansas City suits"}, {"id": "the-kansas-city-media-landscape", "text": "The Kansas City media landscape"}, {"id": "what-stories-travel-in-kansas-city", "text": "What stories travel in Kansas City"}, {"id": "local-state-and-national-coverage-together", "text": "Local, state and national coverage together"}, {"id": "how-it-works-with-dna", "text": "How it works with DNA"}, {"id": "publications-we-place-in-kansas-city", "text": "Publications we place in for Kansas City"}, {"id": "frequently-asked-questions", "text": "Frequently asked questions"}],
  "takeaways": ["The Kansas City Star covers the whole metro area, on both the Missouri and Kansas sides of the state line.", "Stories about engineering, logistics, animal health, technology and food culture tend to resonate with Kansas City readers.", "DNA develops the story, writes it to each publication's standard and manages the placement, and you approve every word before it goes live."],
