  "outlets": ["detroit-free-press", "detroit-news"],
  "body": "<p>A PR agency in Michigan gets your business into the publications that your customers, partners and future staff already trust. For a Detroit mobility start-up or an automotive supplier that could mean the Detroit Free Press or The Detroit News. For a family business in Holland, a resort near Petoskey or a manufacturer in Battle Creek it is more likely the local daily read across the community. We work out who you need to reach, find the angle that interests them, and write the piece to suit each title.</p><p>We work with Michigan businesses remotely, because good placement depends on understanding the publications and writing well. We develop the story with you, write it to the standard of the publication, manage the placement, and you approve every word before it goes live.</p><h2 id=\"who-pr-in-michigan-suits\">Who PR in Michigan suits</h2><p>Michigan coverage works especially well for:</p><ul><li><strong>Automotive, mobility and battery businesses</strong>, from suppliers in Macomb and Oakland counties to electric vehicle start-ups.</li><li><strong>Manufacturers and engineering firms</strong> across south and west Michigan.</li><li><strong>Law firms and professional services</strong> that want visibility with peers and clients.</li><li><strong>Food, farm and drinks producers</strong>, including fruit growers, breweries and wineries.</li><li><strong>Tourism and hospitality businesses</strong> on the lakeshore, in northern Michigan and in the Upper Peninsula.</li></ul><h2 id=\"the-michigan-media-landscape\">The Michigan media landscape</h2><p>Detroit has two major dailies, the Detroit Free Press and The Detroit News, both read well beyond the city. Metro Times covers Detroit's culture, food and nightlife. The suburbs have their own strong titles: The Oakland Press for Oakland County, the Macomb Daily for Macomb County, The News-Herald for the Downriver communities and The Monroe News just to the south. The Times Herald covers Port Huron and the Blue Water area, and the Livingston Daily serves one of the fastest-growing counties in the state.</p><p>The Lansing State Journal covers the capital, state government and Michigan State University. In the south and west, the Battle Creek Enquirer, the Holland Sentinel, the Sturgis Journal, The Daily Telegram in Adrian and the Hillsdale and Coldwater papers serve smaller cities with loyal readers. Up north, the Petoskey News-Review, the Cheboygan Daily Tribune and The Sault News cover resort country and the Upper Peninsula. For legal audiences, Michigan Lawyers Weekly reaches attorneys across the state.</p><h2 id=\"what-stories-travel-in-michigan\">What stories travel in Michigan</h2><p>The car industry is still the biggest story in Michigan, and the shift to electric vehicles, batteries and new mobility technology has opened fresh angles for suppliers and start-ups. Readers follow which companies are investing, hiring and retooling. Detroit's revival, with new businesses, restaurants and housing in the city, is another strong theme.</p><p>Beyond the auto sector, Michigan has a long history in food, from breakfast cereal in Battle Creek to cherries and apples along the western shore. Furniture and design have deep roots around Holland and Grand Rapids. The universities in Ann Arbor, East Lansing and Mount Pleasant produce research and spinouts. Tourism gives northern businesses natural timing, from summer on the Great Lakes to Mackinac Island and autumn colour, and the Soo Locks are part of the identity of Sault Ste. Marie.</p><h2 id=\"local-state-and-national-coverage-together\">Local, state and national coverage together</h2><p>Many Michigan companies sell across North America, especially in manufacturing and automotive supply. A feature in your local daily builds trust with your community and job applicants. A piece in one of the Detroit papers signals that you are a serious Michigan business. National coverage then supports sales and partnerships further afield. We plan these together so each article strengthens the next.</p><h2 id=\"how-it-works-with-dna\">How it works with DNA</h2><p>We begin with a call about your business, your customers and where you want to be seen. We then suggest a shortlist of Michigan and national publications with an angle for each. Our writers draft the article in the style of the title it is going into, and you review it, request changes and approve it. Nothing goes live without your sign-off. We manage the placement and send you the published article, usually within weeks rather than days.</p><h2 id=\"publications-we-place-in-michigan\">Publications we place in across Michigan</h2>\n<p>A selection of the titles we place clients in. Where a title has its own page, it explains what it publishes and how a feature there works.</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/get-featured-in/detroit-free-press\">Detroit Free Press</a></li><li><a href=\"/get-featured-in/detroit-news\">The Detroit News</a></li><li><strong>Lansing State Journal</strong></li><li><strong>Metro Times</strong></li><li><strong>Macomb Daily</strong></li><li><strong>The Oakland Press</strong></li><li><strong>The Times Herald</strong></li><li><strong>Holland Sentinel</strong></li><li><strong>The News Herald</strong></li><li><strong>The Monroe News</strong></li><li><strong>Petoskey News-Review</strong></li><li><strong>Livingston Daily</strong></li><li><strong>The Daily Telegram</strong></li><li><strong>The Morning Sun</strong></li><li><strong>Cheboygan Daily Tribune</strong></li><li><strong>Battle Creek Enquirer</strong></li><li><strong>Sturgis Journal</strong></li><li><strong>Michigan Lawyers Weekly</strong></li><li><strong>Hillsdale Daily News</strong></li><li><strong>Coldwater Daily Reporter</strong></li><li><strong>The Sault News</strong></li></ul>\n<p>City pages: <a href=\"/pr-in/detroit\">PR agency in Detroit</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"frequently-asked-questions\">Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Do I need a Detroit PR agency for Michigan coverage?</h3><p>No. What matters is understanding the difference between the Detroit dailies, suburban papers and small-city titles, and writing to their standard. We work with Michigan businesses remotely and plan coverage around the communities you serve.</p><h3>How do I get featured in the Detroit Free Press?</h3><p>Start with a story that is clearly about Michigan, such as new jobs, an investment or a product made in the state. We develop that story, write it to the paper's standard, manage the placement and send it to you for approval first.</p><h3>What does a Michigan PR agency do?</h3><p>It finds the newsworthy angle in your business, prepares articles for Michigan and national publications, handles placement and helps you use the coverage in sales, hiring and fundraising.</p>",
  "toc": [{"id": "who-pr-in-michigan-suits", "text": "Who PR in Michigan suits"}, {"id": "the-michigan-media-landscape", "text": "The Michigan media landscape"}, {"id": "what-stories-travel-in-michigan", "text": "What stories travel in Michigan"}, {"id": "local-state-and-national-coverage-together", "text": "Local, state and national coverage together"}, {"id": "how-it-works-with-dna", "text": "How it works with DNA"}, {"id": "publications-we-place-in-michigan", "text": "Publications we place in across Michigan"}, {"id": "frequently-asked-questions", "text": "Frequently asked questions"}],
  "takeaways": ["Michigan coverage combines the Detroit dailies with strong suburban, small-city and northern papers.", "Automotive and mobility, manufacturing, food, universities and tourism give Michigan businesses natural story angles.", "We develop and write each article, manage the placement, and you approve every word before it goes live."],
