  "h1": "PR Agency in Ohio",
  "title": "PR Agency in Ohio: Get Featured in Ohio Newspapers",
  "description": "A PR agency for Ohio businesses: we develop your story for The Columbus Dispatch, Akron and Canton papers and town dailies, and you approve every word.",
  "intro": "Digital Networking Agency works with businesses across Ohio to get them featured in the papers their customers and communities read, from Columbus and Akron to the small cities in between.",
  "outlets": ["the-columbus-dispatch"],
  "body": "<p>A PR agency in Ohio gets your business written about in the publications that matter to the people you serve. For a Columbus technology or insurance firm that might be The Columbus Dispatch or Columbus CEO. For a manufacturer in Mansfield, a family business in Wooster or a marina near Port Clinton it is more likely the local daily that readers have trusted for generations. We work out which readers count, find the angle in your work that interests them, and write the piece to fit the title.</p><p>We work with Ohio businesses remotely, because placement depends on knowing the publications and writing well. We develop the story with you, write it to the standard of each title, manage the placement, and you approve every word before it goes live.</p><h2 id=\"who-pr-in-ohio-suits\">Who PR in Ohio suits</h2><p>Ohio coverage tends to work best for:</p><ul><li><strong>Manufacturers and industrial suppliers</strong>, from automotive and steel to polymers and machinery.</li><li><strong>Technology, insurance and retail businesses in Columbus</strong>, one of the fastest-growing cities in the Midwest.</li><li><strong>Healthcare providers and medical firms</strong> in the larger metro areas.</li><li><strong>Family businesses in small cities and rural counties</strong> where the local paper is still central to community life.</li><li><strong>Tourism and hospitality businesses</strong> along Lake Erie and in Amish country.</li></ul><h2 id=\"the-ohio-media-landscape\">The Ohio media landscape</h2><p>Ohio has an unusually deep bench of local dailies. In central Ohio, The Columbus Dispatch is the paper of record, while Columbus Monthly and Columbus CEO cover the city's lifestyle and business communities. Around Columbus, the Newark Advocate, the Lancaster Eagle-Gazette, The Marion Star and the Chillicothe Gazette serve fast-changing towns where many residents now commute into the capital.</p><p>In north-east Ohio, the Akron Beacon Journal, CantonRep, the Massillon Independent, The Alliance Review and the Kent Ravenna Record-Courier cover a region with deep industrial roots. The Morning Journal covers Lorain and the News-Herald covers Lake County. Further south and west, The Daily Record in Wooster, the Times Reporter in Tuscarawas County, the Coshocton Tribune, the Mansfield News Journal and the Fremont News Messenger serve smaller cities with loyal readerships. This spread means an Ohio plan can be precisely targeted to the communities you want to reach.</p><h2 id=\"what-stories-travel-in-ohio\">What stories travel in Ohio</h2><p>Ohio readers respond to stories about making things and creating jobs. Manufacturing, automotive supply, steel and the polymer industry that grew out of Akron's tyre heritage all give businesses a natural angle. The large semiconductor investment in Licking County and the growth around New Albany have made technology and construction a major theme in central Ohio.</p><p>Columbus brings stories about insurance, retail, start-ups and Ohio State University. Healthcare is a major employer across the state. Tourism has its own seasons, from Lake Erie islands and marinas around Port Clinton to Amish country near Wooster, Coshocton and Holmes County, and Canton draws football fans year round. Agriculture remains important in the north-west and across rural counties, and stories about farm businesses and food producers are welcomed by local papers.</p><h2 id=\"local-state-and-national-coverage-together\">Local, state and national coverage together</h2><p>Many Ohio businesses sell across the Midwest and the country. A feature in your home-town daily builds trust with customers and future employees. A piece in a Columbus business title tells partners you are a serious Ohio company. National coverage then supports sales further afield. We plan these together, so each article strengthens the next and gives you credible material for your website, proposals and recruitment.</p><h2 id=\"how-it-works-with-dna\">How it works with DNA</h2><p>We begin with a conversation about your business, your customers and where you want to be seen. We suggest a shortlist of Ohio and national publications with an angle for each. Our writers draft the article in the style of the title, and you review it, ask for changes and approve it. Nothing goes live without your sign-off. We manage the placement and send you the published article, usually within weeks rather than days.</p><h2 id=\"publications-we-place-in-ohio\">Publications we place in across Ohio</h2>\n<p>A selection of the titles we place clients in. Where a title has its own page, it explains what it publishes and how a feature there works.</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/get-featured-in/the-columbus-dispatch\">The Columbus Dispatch</a></li><li><strong>Cincinnati News</strong></li><li><strong>Akron Beacon Journal</strong></li><li><strong>CantonRep</strong></li><li><strong>Mansfield News Journal</strong></li><li><strong>News-Herald Ohio News</strong></li><li><strong>The Daily Record</strong></li><li><strong>Chillicothe Gazette</strong></li><li><strong>The Marion Star</strong></li><li><strong>Morning Journal</strong></li><li><strong>Zanesville Times Recorder</strong></li><li><strong>Kent Ravenna Record-Courier</strong></li><li><strong>Newark Advocate</strong></li><li><strong>Lancaster Eagle-Gazette</strong></li><li><strong>Times Reporter</strong></li><li><strong>The Alliance Review</strong></li><li><strong>Columbus Monthly</strong></li><li><strong>The Daily Jeffersonian</strong></li><li><strong>Ashland Times Gazette</strong></li><li><strong>Massillon Independent</strong></li><li><strong>Fremont News Messenger</strong></li><li><strong>Bucyrus Telegraph-Forum</strong></li><li><strong>Coshocton Tribune</strong></li><li><strong>Port Clinton News Herald</strong></li><li><strong>Columbus CEO</strong></li></ul>\n<p>City pages: <a href=\"/pr-in/columbus\">PR agency in Columbus</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"frequently-asked-questions\">Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Do I need a Columbus PR agency for Ohio coverage?</h3><p>No. What matters is understanding Ohio's regional papers and writing to their standard. We work with Ohio businesses remotely and plan coverage around the towns and cities you serve.</p><h3>How do I get featured in Ohio newspapers?</h3><p>Start with a story that is clearly about Ohio, such as new jobs, an expansion or a product made in the state, then match it to the paper that covers your area. We develop the story, write it, manage the placement and send it to you for approval first.</p><h3>What does an Ohio PR agency do?</h3><p>It finds the newsworthy angle in your business, prepares articles for Ohio and national publications, handles placement and helps you use the coverage in sales, hiring and fundraising.</p>",
