  "intro": "We help Raleigh businesses get featured in The News & Observer and established papers across North Carolina. We shape the story, write it to each title's standard and manage the placement, and you approve every word.",
  "outlets": ["charlotte-observer"],
  "body": "<p>A PR agency in Raleigh helps your business reach the people who shape the Research Triangle: customers, university partners, investors, policymakers and skilled hires. The aim is a clear, credible story about your company in a publication those readers already trust, written so it informs rather than sells.</p><p>Digital Networking Agency works with businesses in Raleigh remotely. We develop the story, write it to each publication's standard, manage the placement and send it to you for review, so you approve every word before it goes live. It is a practical way for a Raleigh company to build a track record of coverage without hiring a press team.</p><h2 id=\"who-pr-in-raleigh-suits\">Who PR in Raleigh suits</h2><p>Raleigh combines the role of state capital with a research-led economy, and coverage helps most where a business sits at the meeting point of the two. We often work with:</p><ul><li><strong>Life sciences and biotech companies</strong> connected to the Research Triangle Park cluster.</li><li><strong>Software and technology firms</strong>, including open-source and enterprise businesses, competing for talent in the Triangle.</li><li><strong>University spin-outs and founders</strong> with roots at NC State, Duke or UNC.</li><li><strong>Firms that work with state government</strong>, from consultancies to contractors and advocacy groups.</li><li><strong>Property, healthcare and professional services businesses</strong> serving a fast-growing population.</li></ul><h2 id=\"the-raleigh-media-landscape\">The Raleigh media landscape</h2><p>The News &amp; Observer is Raleigh's main daily newspaper and a long-standing voice on politics, business and community life in the Triangle and across North Carolina. Because the paper sits in the state capital, its coverage reaches people working in government, education and research as well as everyday Raleigh readers. A feature there is a strong, shareable piece of credibility for any Raleigh business.</p><p>Nearby, The Herald Sun covers Durham, home of Duke and a large share of the Triangle's start-up and life sciences activity. Further across the state, the Charlotte Observer, the News &amp; Record in Greensboro and the Winston-Salem Journal reach North Carolina's other major business centres, which is useful if your customers or partners are spread across the state.</p><h2 id=\"what-stories-travel-in-raleigh\">What stories travel in Raleigh</h2><p>Raleigh readers respond to stories about research turning into jobs, growth reshaping the city and decisions made at the state capital. Angles we develop regularly include:</p><ul><li>Research and discoveries moving from the lab into real products and companies.</li><li>Technology firms growing in the Triangle and the talent they are hiring.</li><li>Agricultural technology and food innovation, building on North Carolina's farming base.</li><li>Policy, education and public sector work tied to the state government.</li><li>Companies relocating to Raleigh or expanding their presence in the Triangle.</li></ul><p>A good story also needs a reason to run now. We look for the timely detail in your business, such as a launch, a funding round, a partnership or a founder's considered view on growth and housing in Wake County.</p><h2 id=\"local-state-and-national-coverage-together\">Local, state and national coverage together</h2><p>Raleigh businesses often serve the whole state and beyond, so we plan coverage in layers. The News &amp; Observer establishes you at home in the Triangle. Placements in titles such as The Herald Sun, the Charlotte Observer or The Fayetteville Observer extend that reach to other North Carolina communities. National business coverage then helps when you are speaking to investors, partners or customers in other states.</p><h2 id=\"how-it-works-with-dna\">How it works with DNA</h2><p>We begin with a conversation about your business and what you want coverage to achieve in Raleigh and further afield. We then recommend the publications that fit, develop the angle and write the article in the style each title expects. You review the draft and approve every word. After that we manage the placement through to publication and share the live coverage with you. The process takes weeks rather than days.</p><h2 id=\"publications-we-place-in-raleigh\">Publications we place in for Raleigh</h2>\n<p>These are the Raleigh titles we place clients in. Where a title has its own page, it explains what it publishes and how a feature there works.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>The News &amp; Observer</strong></li></ul>\n<h3>Across North Carolina</h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/get-featured-in/charlotte-observer\">Charlotte Observer</a></li><li><strong>The Citizen-Times</strong></li><li><strong>Wilmington Star-News</strong></li><li><strong>Winston-Salem Journal</strong></li><li><strong>The Fayetteville Observer</strong></li><li><strong>News &amp; Record</strong></li><li><strong>Gaston Gazette</strong></li><li><strong>Hickory Daily Record</strong></li><li><strong>The Herald Sun</strong></li><li><strong>Shelby Star</strong></li><li><strong>The Morganton News Herald</strong></li><li><strong>Statesville Record &amp; Landmark</strong></li><li><strong>The McDowell News</strong></li><li><strong>The Independent Tribune</strong></li><li><strong>North Carolina Lawyers</strong></li></ul>\n<p>See every title we place in across the state on our <a href=\"/pr-in/north-carolina\">PR agency in North Carolina</a> page.</p>\n<h2 id=\"frequently-asked-questions\">Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Do I need a Raleigh PR agency to get covered locally?</h3><p>No. What matters is knowing Triangle and North Carolina media and writing to each publication's standard. We work with Raleigh businesses remotely and manage the whole process for you.</p><h3>How do I get featured in The News &amp; Observer?</h3><p>Bring a timely story with clear relevance to Raleigh or the Triangle, such as growth, research, hiring or a new product. We develop it, write it to the paper's standard and manage the placement, and you approve the final text.</p><h3>What does a PR agency in Raleigh do?</h3><p>It finds the newsworthy angle in your business, prepares articles for Raleigh and North Carolina publications and handles each placement. With DNA, nothing goes live until you have approved every word.</p>",
