  "h1": "PR Agency in San Diego",
  "title": "PR Agency in San Diego: Get Featured in Local Media",
  "description": "A PR agency for San Diego businesses: we shape your story, write it to each title's standard and place it in local and California media, with your approval.",
  "intro": "San Diego mixes world-class research, a large military presence and a relaxed coastal lifestyle, and its business stories reflect all three. We work with businesses in San Diego to turn their work into coverage that local customers, partners and investors can find.",
  "outlets": ["hollywood-life", "hollywood-reporter", "la-weekly", "oc-register", "san-diego-union-tribune"],
  "body": "<p>A PR agency in San Diego helps you get your business into the publications that San Diegans read, from the beach communities to North County and the South Bay. The work is finding the story in what you already do, writing it in the style of a particular title and placing it where it keeps appearing when people search for you.</p><p>We work with San Diego businesses remotely and handle the full process. We develop the story with you, write it to the publication's standard, manage the placement, and you approve every word before it goes live. You get coverage you can share with clients, use in investor and partner conversations, and point to when a new contact looks you up.</p><h2 id=\"who-pr-in-san-diego-suits\">Who PR in San Diego suits</h2><p>San Diego's business community is smaller and more connected than Los Angeles, which makes local reputation especially valuable. PR in San Diego tends to suit:</p><ul><li>Biotech, life sciences and medical device companies around Torrey Pines and Sorrento Valley</li><li>Wireless, software and defence technology firms</li><li>Breweries, restaurants and food brands in a city known for craft beer</li><li>Hotels, tour operators and hospitality businesses that depend on visitors</li><li>Property, construction and professional firms serving a coastal market</li></ul><h2 id=\"the-san-diego-media-landscape\">The San Diego media landscape</h2><p>The <strong>San Diego Union Tribune</strong> is the region's main daily newspaper and the title most San Diegans associate with local news. Coverage there carries weight with customers, employers and institutions across the county.</p><p>The <strong>San Diego Reader</strong>, a long-running free weekly, is known for its coverage of food, music, arts and neighbourhood life, and suits restaurants, breweries and venues with a strong local identity. <strong>San Diego Weekly</strong> follows local news and the people behind the city's businesses. We choose each title by who reads it, so a biotech milestone and a new taproom in North Park end up in front of the right readers.</p><h2 id=\"what-stories-travel-in-san-diego\">What stories travel in San Diego</h2><p>San Diego's economy rests on several strong pillars. The US Navy and Marine Corps have a major presence, supporting a large defence and shipbuilding sector. The research institutions around La Jolla, including UC San Diego and the Scripps institutes, have made the region a leading centre for biotech and life sciences, and the city has deep roots in wireless technology. Tourism, from the beaches to the zoo and Balboa Park, and close ties with Tijuana across the border round it out.</p><p>Stories that travel in San Diego often link innovation with place: a startup spun out of local research, a veteran-founded business, a brewery growing out of a neighbourhood taproom, or a company working across the border. San Diego readers value the city's balance of ambition and lifestyle, so we keep stories specific to how your business fits into it.</p><h2 id=\"local-state-and-national-coverage-together\">Local, state and national coverage together</h2><p>Many San Diego businesses sell across Southern California and the rest of the state. A San Diego title builds trust at home, while the <strong>LA Times</strong> and the <strong>OC Register</strong> reach readers up the coast, and <strong>Business Journal Silicon Valley</strong> speaks to the Bay Area technology and investment community. We plan placements together, so one story can give you a San Diego presence and California-wide reach.</p><h2 id=\"how-it-works-with-dna\">How it works with DNA</h2><ul><li><strong>Story:</strong> we talk through your business and find the San Diego angle worth publishing.</li><li><strong>Writing:</strong> we draft the piece to the style and standard of the chosen title.</li><li><strong>Approval:</strong> you review and approve every word before it goes live.</li><li><strong>Placement:</strong> we manage the placement and send you the live article.</li></ul><p>Most placements take weeks rather than days, depending on the title and how quickly drafts are signed off.</p><h2 id=\"publications-we-place-in-san-diego\">Publications we place in for San Diego</h2>\n<p>These are the San Diego titles we place clients in. Where a title has its own page, it explains what it publishes and how a feature there works.</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/get-featured-in/san-diego-union-tribune\">San Diego Union Tribune</a></li><li><strong>San Diego Reader</strong></li><li><strong>San Diego Weekly</strong></li></ul>\n<h3>Across California</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>LA Times</strong></li><li><a href=\"/get-featured-in/hollywood-reporter\">The Hollywood Reporter</a></li><li><strong>Business Journal Silicon Valley</strong></li><li><strong>Mercury News</strong></li><li><a href=\"/get-featured-in/oc-register\">OC Register</a></li><li><strong>The Sacramento Bee</strong></li><li><strong>Flaunt Magazine</strong></li><li><a href=\"/get-featured-in/hollywood-life\">Hollywood Life</a></li><li><strong>East Bay Times</strong></li><li><strong>LA Magazine</strong></li><li><strong>The Fresno Bee</strong></li><li><a href=\"/get-featured-in/la-weekly\">LA Weekly</a></li><li><strong>VC Star</strong></li><li><strong>The Desert Sun</strong></li><li><strong>San Luis Obispo Tribune</strong></li></ul>\n<p>See every title we place in across the state on our <a href=\"/pr-in/california\">PR agency in California</a> page.</p>\n<h2 id=\"frequently-asked-questions\">Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Do I need a San Diego PR firm to get local press?</h3><p>No. What matters is knowing which San Diego titles reach your customers and writing to their standard. We work with San Diego businesses remotely, and the coverage reads the same to your audience.</p><h3>How do I get featured in the San Diego Union Tribune?</h3><p>Start with a story that has a clear San Diego angle, such as local research, hiring, a new opening or a link to the border region. We shape it, write it to the paper's standard and manage the placement, with your approval first.</p><h3>What does a San Diego PR agency do?</h3><p>A San Diego PR agency turns your business news into stories for local and California titles and handles the placement, so you have coverage that builds trust with customers, partners and investors.</p>",
  "toc": [{"id": "who-pr-in-san-diego-suits", "text": "Who PR in San Diego suits"}, {"id": "the-san-diego-media-landscape", "text": "The San Diego media landscape"}, {"id": "what-stories-travel-in-san-diego", "text": "What stories travel in San Diego"}, {"id": "local-state-and-national-coverage-together", "text": "Local, state and national coverage together"}, {"id": "how-it-works-with-dna", "text": "How it works with DNA"}, {"id": "publications-we-place-in-san-diego", "text": "Publications we place in for San Diego"}, {"id": "frequently-asked-questions", "text": "Frequently asked questions"}],
  "takeaways": ["San Diego coverage works best when it ties to the region's strengths in biotech, defence, wireless technology and tourism.", "The San Diego Union Tribune and the San Diego Reader reach different readers, so the story has to suit the title.", "We develop the story, write it to the publication's standard and manage the placement, and you approve every word."],
  "kind": "city",
  "area": "San Diego, California",
  "pubCount": 18
