  "slug": "tennessee",
  "region": "Tennessee",
  "h1": "PR Agency in Tennessee",
  "title": "PR Agency in Tennessee: Get Featured in Tennessee Media",
  "description": "A PR agency for Tennessee businesses: we develop your story for The Tennessean, the Commercial Appeal and Knox News, manage placement, you approve it.",
  "intro": "Digital Networking Agency works with businesses across Tennessee to get them featured in the papers their customers trust, from Memphis and Nashville to Knoxville and the towns between.",
  "outlets": [],
  "body": "<p>A PR agency in Tennessee gets your business written about in the publications that people in your market already read. For a Nashville healthcare start-up that could be The Tennessean. For a manufacturer near Columbia or a family firm in Jackson it is more likely the local daily that customers and suppliers check every morning. We work out which readers you need, find the part of your story that matters to them, and write it in a way that fits each title.</p><p>We work with Tennessee businesses remotely. Placement depends on knowing the publications and writing well, not on a local desk. We develop the story with you, write it to the standard of the publication, manage the placement, and you approve every word before it goes live.</p><h2 id=\"who-pr-in-tennessee-suits\">Who PR in Tennessee suits</h2><p>Tennessee coverage tends to pay off most for:</p><ul><li><strong>Healthcare and health technology companies</strong> in and around Nashville, which has long been a centre for the industry.</li><li><strong>Music, entertainment and creative businesses</strong> that want recognition beyond the industry itself.</li><li><strong>Automotive and manufacturing suppliers</strong> in Middle and West Tennessee, from Spring Hill and Smyrna to the newer projects near Memphis.</li><li><strong>Logistics and distribution firms</strong> in Memphis, one of the country's great freight hubs.</li><li><strong>Tourism and hospitality businesses</strong> in the Smokies, on the Cumberland Plateau and in the major cities.</li></ul><h2 id=\"the-tennessee-media-landscape\">The Tennessee media landscape</h2><p>Tennessee's media follows its three Grand Divisions. In Middle Tennessee, The Tennessean is the main paper for Nashville and the surrounding counties, with the Daily News Journal covering Murfreesboro and Rutherford County, The Leaf-Chronicle covering Clarksville and the Columbia Daily Herald covering Maury County. These suburban and satellite cities are growing fast, and their papers are read closely by new residents.</p><p>In West Tennessee, the Commercial Appeal is the paper of record for Memphis and the Jackson Sun covers Jackson and the surrounding rural counties. In East Tennessee, Knox News serves Knoxville and the wider region, while The Oakridger covers Oak Ridge, a town shaped by science and federal research. Because each region has its own identity, a strong Tennessee plan usually picks the papers that match where your customers actually are.</p><h2 id=\"what-stories-travel-in-tennessee\">What stories travel in Tennessee</h2><p>The stories that land in Tennessee tie a business to what the state is known for. In Nashville that means music, healthcare and the steady stream of companies relocating to the city. In Memphis it means logistics, distribution and the city's food and music heritage. In Knoxville and Oak Ridge, research, energy and advanced materials give technical firms a natural way in.</p><p>Manufacturing is a strong theme across the state. Automotive plants and their suppliers, battery and electric vehicle projects, and new factory jobs in smaller towns all interest local readers. Tourism stories work well in the east, where the Great Smoky Mountains draw visitors year round, and Tennessee whiskey has its own loyal audience. In Clarksville, businesses that serve military families around Fort Campbell have a clear local angle.</p><h2 id=\"local-state-and-national-coverage-together\">Local, state and national coverage together</h2><p>Tennessee companies often sell across the South and beyond, so it helps to build coverage in layers. A feature in your local paper builds trust with the community and with recruits. A piece in one of the big-city dailies shows partners that you are an established Tennessee business. National coverage then gives you something to point to with customers elsewhere. We plan these together, so the local story supports the wider one rather than standing alone.</p><h2 id=\"how-it-works-with-dna\">How it works with DNA</h2><p>We start with a conversation about your business, your customers and the parts of Tennessee, or the wider country, where you want to be seen. We suggest publications and a story angle for each, and our writers draft the article in the style of the title it is going into. You review it, ask for any changes and approve it. Nothing goes live without your sign-off. We manage the placement and send you the published piece, usually within weeks rather than days.</p><h2 id=\"publications-we-place-in-tennessee\">Publications we place in across Tennessee</h2>\n<p>A selection of the titles we place clients in. Where a title has its own page, it explains what it publishes and how a feature there works.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>The Tennessean</strong></li><li><strong>Knox News</strong></li><li><strong>Commercial Appeal</strong></li><li><strong>Columbia Daily Herald</strong></li><li><strong>The Leaf Chronicle</strong></li><li><strong>Oakridger</strong></li><li><strong>Daily News Journal</strong></li><li><strong>Jackson Sun</strong></li></ul>\n<p>City pages: <a href=\"/pr-in/nashville\">PR agency in Nashville</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"frequently-asked-questions\">Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Do I need a PR agency in Nashville to get Tennessee coverage?</h3><p>No. What counts is understanding how Tennessee media differs between Memphis, Nashville and Knoxville, and writing to each paper's standard. We work with Tennessee businesses remotely and plan coverage around the regions you serve.</p><h3>How do I get featured in Tennessee newspapers?</h3><p>Start with a story that is clearly about Tennessee, such as new jobs, an expansion or a local founder, then match it to the paper that covers your area. We develop that story, write it, manage the placement and send it to you for approval first.</p><h3>What does a Tennessee PR agency do?</h3><p>It finds the newsworthy angle in your business, prepares articles for Tennessee and national publications, handles placement and helps you use the coverage in sales, recruitment and fundraising.</p>",
  "toc": [{"id": "who-pr-in-tennessee-suits", "text": "Who PR in Tennessee suits"}, {"id": "the-tennessee-media-landscape", "text": "The Tennessee media landscape"}, {"id": "what-stories-travel-in-tennessee", "text": "What stories travel in Tennessee"}, {"id": "local-state-and-national-coverage-together", "text": "Local, state and national coverage together"}, {"id": "how-it-works-with-dna", "text": "How it works with DNA"}, {"id": "publications-we-place-in-tennessee", "text": "Publications we place in across Tennessee"}, {"id": "frequently-asked-questions", "text": "Frequently asked questions"}],
  "takeaways": ["Tennessee media follows the state's three regions, so coverage is planned around Memphis, Nashville and Knoxville separately.", "Healthcare, music, logistics, automotive manufacturing and tourism give Tennessee businesses natural story angles.", "We develop and write each article, manage the placement, and you approve every word before it goes live."],
  "kind": "state",
  "area": "Tennessee",
  "pubCount": 8
