  "title": "PR Agency in Bahrain: Get Featured in Gulf Business Media",
  "description": "A PR agency for Bahrain businesses: we shape your story and place it in Trade Arabia, Gulf Construction, Oil & Gas News and other respected Gulf titles.",
  "intro": "DNA works with companies and executives in Bahrain to turn real business news into features in the Gulf trade and industry titles that decision-makers read, with your approval on every word.",
  "outlets": [],
  "body": "<p>A PR agency in Bahrain helps your company reach the people who make decisions in your sector, through the publications they already read. In a market where so much business depends on relationships and reputation, a well-placed feature gives clients, partners and investors a credible reason to take your call.</p><p>We work with businesses in Bahrain from the first idea to the published feature. We develop the story, write it to the publication's standard, manage the placement, and you approve every word before it goes live. You end up with coverage you can share in tenders, proposals and investor conversations across the Gulf.</p><h2 id=\"who-pr-in-bahrain-suits\">Who PR in Bahrain suits</h2><p>PR in Bahrain suits companies that sell to other businesses or to government. That includes contractors and engineering firms, energy and industrial suppliers, banks and fintech companies, logistics operators, hotels and hospitality groups, and professional services firms advising clients across the region. It also suits executives who want a clear profile as they take on a regional role or lead a company into Saudi Arabia and the wider Gulf.</p><h2 id=\"the-bahrain-media-landscape\">The Bahrain media landscape</h2><p>Bahrain has long been a publishing hub for Gulf business media, with a group of trade titles read well beyond the kingdom's borders. Alongside them, national newspapers such as the Gulf Daily News in English and Akhbar Al Khaleej and Al Ayam in Arabic cover local affairs, government announcements and company news.</p><p>The trade titles are where specialist stories land best. Trade Arabia covers business news across the Gulf, Gulf Construction is read by contractors, consultants and developers, Oil &amp; Gas News serves the energy sector, Gulf Industry Online covers manufacturing and industrial projects, and Travel &amp; Tourism News reaches the hospitality and travel trade. Each has a specific readership, so a story is shaped around what those readers need to know rather than written once and sent everywhere.</p><h2 id=\"what-stories-travel-in-bahrain\">What stories travel in Bahrain</h2><p>The best Bahraini stories connect to what the economy is known for. Banking and financial services have been central for decades, and the Central Bank of Bahrain's fintech sandbox has made the kingdom a natural base for payments and digital finance companies. Oil refining and aluminium production anchor heavy industry, and suppliers to those sectors have plenty to say about efficiency, safety and new technology.</p><p>Construction and infrastructure projects, from waterfront developments to industrial zones, suit Gulf Construction and Gulf Industry Online. Bahrain's causeway link to Saudi Arabia gives logistics and trade companies a strong regional angle. Tourism and events, including the Formula One Grand Prix at Sakhir, create openings for hotels, restaurants and leisure operators in travel titles.</p><ul><li><strong>Project and contract news</strong> for construction and industrial readers</li><li><strong>Leadership and expansion stories</strong> for business readers across the Gulf</li><li><strong>Hospitality and destination stories</strong> for the travel trade</li></ul><h2 id=\"local-national-and-regional-coverage-together\">Local, national and regional coverage together</h2><p>Bahrain is a small market with a regional outlook, so most companies need to be visible in more than one country. Coverage in a Gulf-wide trade title reaches buyers in Saudi Arabia, the United Arab Emirates, Kuwait, Qatar and Oman, while national newspapers keep you visible at home with government, regulators and local partners.</p><p>We plan placements so they support each other. A project story in a trade title and a leadership profile in a business title give different audiences two reasons to remember your name, without repeating the same article.</p><h2 id=\"how-it-works-with-dna\">How it works with DNA</h2><p>We begin with a conversation about your company, your customers and what you want the coverage to do. We then recommend the titles that fit and the angle for each. Next we develop the story, write it to the publication's standard, manage the placement, and you approve every word before it goes live.</p><p>Technical accuracy matters in trade media, so we check terminology, project names and job titles with you before anything is finalised. Timelines depend on each title's schedule, and most placements take weeks rather than days.</p><h2 id=\"publications-we-place-in-bahrain\">Publications we place in across Bahrain</h2>\n<p>A selection of the titles we place clients in. Where a title has its own page, it explains what it publishes and how a feature there works.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>ABC</strong></li><li><strong>Trade Arabia</strong></li><li><strong>Gulf Construction</strong></li><li><strong>Oil &amp; Gas News</strong></li><li><strong>Gulf Industry Online</strong></li><li><strong>Travel &amp; Tourism News</strong></li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"frequently-asked-questions\">Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Do I need a PR agency based in Bahrain?</h3><p>No. What matters is knowing which titles your buyers read and how to write for them. We work with businesses in Bahrain remotely and manage the whole process, from the angle to the approved feature.</p><h3>How do I get featured in Bahrain trade publications?</h3><p>Start with news that matters to the title's readers, such as a contract, a new facility, a market entry or a clear view on an industry challenge. We shape that into a story, write it to the publication's standard and manage the placement.</p><h3>What does a PR agency in Bahrain do?</h3><p>It finds the newsworthy angle in your business, matches it to the right publications and turns it into coverage. With DNA that means planning, writing, placement and your sign-off on every word.</p>",
  "toc": [{"id": "who-pr-in-bahrain-suits", "text": "Who PR in Bahrain suits"}, {"id": "the-bahrain-media-landscape", "text": "The Bahrain media landscape"}, {"id": "what-stories-travel-in-bahrain", "text": "What stories travel in Bahrain"}, {"id": "local-national-and-regional-coverage-together", "text": "Local, national and regional coverage together"}, {"id": "how-it-works-with-dna", "text": "How it works with DNA"}, {"id": "publications-we-place-in-bahrain", "text": "Publications we place in across Bahrain"}, {"id": "frequently-asked-questions", "text": "Frequently asked questions"}],
  "takeaways": ["A PR agency in Bahrain places your story in Gulf titles such as Trade Arabia, Gulf Construction, Oil & Gas News and Travel & Tourism News.", "Strong Bahraini stories tie to finance and fintech, refining, aluminium, construction, logistics and tourism.", "DNA develops the story, writes it to each publication's standard and manages the placement, and you approve every word before it goes live."],
