  "h1": "PR Agency in Iowa",
  "title": "PR Agency in Iowa: Get Featured in Iowa Newspapers",
  "description": "A PR agency for Iowa businesses: we develop your story and place it in Des Moines, Sioux City, Iowa City and Quad Cities media, with your approval first.",
  "intro": "We work with businesses across Iowa to win a place in the newspapers their communities read, from Des Moines and Iowa City to Sioux City, Mason City and the Quad Cities.",
  "outlets": ["des-moines-register"],
  "body": "<p>A PR agency in Iowa helps your business get written about in the newspapers Iowans read and trust. In a state where many people still follow their regional daily closely, a well-placed article can do a lot: it introduces you to customers, reassures partners and lenders, and gives anyone who searches your name something solid to find.</p><p>DNA works with businesses in Iowa remotely. We look for the story in what you do, write it to the standard of the publication it is going to, manage the placement and keep you in control throughout. You approve every word before anything goes live, and you receive the published article to use in sales, recruiting and on your own website.</p><h2 id=\"who-pr-in-iowa-suits\">Who PR in Iowa suits</h2><p>Iowa businesses that benefit most from coverage tend to have a clear local audience and a story worth telling. We often work with:</p><ul><li><strong>Agribusiness and food companies</strong>, from seed and equipment to processing and specialty products.</li><li><strong>Insurance and financial services firms</strong> in and around Des Moines.</li><li><strong>Manufacturers</strong> in Waterloo, Cedar Rapids, Muscatine and the Quad Cities.</li><li><strong>Healthcare, legal and professional practices</strong> that rely on standing in their own community.</li><li><strong>Founders and start-ups</strong> connected to Iowa State and the University of Iowa.</li></ul><h2 id=\"the-iowa-media-landscape\">The Iowa media landscape</h2><p>The Des Moines Register is the state's best-known newspaper and covers business, politics and agriculture from the capital. Around it sits a network of established regional dailies, each with a loyal readership. The Sioux City Journal covers the north-west of the state and the area where Iowa meets Nebraska and South Dakota. The Iowa City Press-Citizen serves the university city, and The Ames Tribune covers Ames and Story County.</p><p>In the north-east, the Waterloo-Cedar Falls Courier covers the Cedar Valley, and the Globe Gazette serves Mason City and north Iowa. On the eastern edge, the Quad-City Times and the Moline Dispatch &amp; Rock Island Argus cover a metro area shared with Illinois, while The Muscatine Journal serves the river town of Muscatine. In the west, The Daily Nonpareil covers Council Bluffs and its links to Omaha. Because readership is spread out, the right mix depends on where your customers actually live.</p><h2 id=\"what-stories-travel-in-iowa\">What stories travel in Iowa</h2><p>Agriculture shapes Iowa's economy and its news. Corn, soybeans, pork and ethanol are everyday subjects, so a business that can explain its role in farming, food or rural life has a natural audience. Farm equipment manufacturing in the Cedar Valley and the Quad Cities, and meat and food processing in places such as Sioux City, give manufacturing stories a strong local angle.</p><p>Des Moines is a major centre for insurance and financial services, which makes stories about growth, hiring and leadership in that sector a good fit. Wind energy has become a notable part of the state's identity. Iowa State University in Ames and the University of Iowa in Iowa City generate research, engineering and healthcare stories, and Iowa City's literary reputation gives creative businesses a hook. The more clearly a story connects to these strengths, the more it reads as news rather than promotion.</p><h2 id=\"local-state-and-national-coverage-together\">Local, state and national coverage together</h2><p>Iowa coverage works well in layers. A feature in the paper that serves your town builds trust with nearby customers. A Des Moines placement signals to the rest of the state that you are an established business. National coverage then adds reach if you sell beyond Iowa or are speaking to investors. Planned together, each placement supports the others.</p><h2 id=\"how-it-works-with-dna\">How it works with DNA</h2><p>We start by learning about your business, your customers and the parts of Iowa that matter to you. We recommend the titles that fit, develop the angle and write the article to that publication's style. You review the draft, ask for any changes and approve the final version. We then manage the placement and send you the live article. Plan on weeks rather than days.</p><h2 id=\"publications-we-place-in-iowa\">Publications we place in across Iowa</h2>\n<p>A selection of the titles we place clients in. Where a title has its own page, it explains what it publishes and how a feature there works.</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/get-featured-in/des-moines-register\">The Des Moines Register</a></li><li><strong>Quad-City Times</strong></li><li><strong>Sioux City Journal</strong></li><li><strong>Iowa City Press-Citizen</strong></li><li><strong>Waterloo-Cedar Falls Courier</strong></li><li><strong>The Ames Tribune</strong></li><li><strong>Moline Dispatch &amp; Rock Island Argus</strong></li><li><strong>The Daily Nonpareil</strong></li><li><strong>The Muscatine Journal</strong></li><li><strong>Globe Gazette</strong></li></ul>\n<p>City pages: <a href=\"/pr-in/des-moines\">PR agency in Des Moines</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"frequently-asked-questions\">Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Do I need a PR agency based in Iowa?</h3><p>No. What matters is understanding Iowa's regional papers and what their readers want. We work with Iowa businesses remotely and plan coverage across Des Moines and the regional dailies.</p><h3>How do I get featured in the Des Moines Register?</h3><p>Start with a story that matters to Iowa readers, such as local jobs, agriculture, insurance or a new product made in the state. We develop the angle, write it to the paper's standard and manage the placement after your approval.</p><h3>Which Iowa newspapers should my business appear in?</h3><p>That depends on where your customers are. A Cedar Valley manufacturer may start with the Waterloo-Cedar Falls Courier, while a western Iowa business may look first at the Sioux City Journal or The Daily Nonpareil.</p>",
  "toc": [{"id": "who-pr-in-iowa-suits", "text": "Who PR in Iowa suits"}, {"id": "the-iowa-media-landscape", "text": "The Iowa media landscape"}, {"id": "what-stories-travel-in-iowa", "text": "What stories travel in Iowa"}, {"id": "local-state-and-national-coverage-together", "text": "Local, state and national coverage together"}, {"id": "how-it-works-with-dna", "text": "How it works with DNA"}, {"id": "publications-we-place-in-iowa", "text": "Publications we place in across Iowa"}, {"id": "frequently-asked-questions", "text": "Frequently asked questions"}],
  "takeaways": ["Iowa coverage is spread across respected regional dailies, so a plan that reaches several cities usually beats a single Des Moines placement.", "Stories tied to agriculture, food processing, insurance, manufacturing and the state's universities fit how Iowa papers cover the state.", "DNA develops the story, writes it to each publication's standard and manages placement, and you approve every word before it goes live."],
  "kind": "state",
