  "slug": "montreal",
  "region": "Montreal",
  "h1": "PR Agency in Montreal",
  "title": "PR Agency in Montreal: Get Featured in Local Media",
  "description": "A PR agency for Montreal businesses: we develop your story and place it in the Montreal Gazette, Cult Montreal and national Canadian titles you can trust.",
  "intro": "DNA PR works with businesses in Montreal that want to reach the city's English-language readers and audiences across Canada. We shape the story, write it to each publication's standard and manage the placement, and you approve every word.",
  "outlets": ["calgary-herald", "edmonton-journal", "financial-post", "investing-com", "montreal-gazette", "national-post", "ottawa-citizen", "toronto-sun", "vancouver-sun"],
  "body": "<p>A PR agency in Montreal helps your business appear in the publications that shape how people in the city and beyond see you. It finds the story in your work, writes it to suit each outlet and manages the placement, whether that is the Montreal Gazette, Cult Montreal or a national title such as the National Post or the Financial Post.</p><p>For many Montreal companies the goal is credibility with a wider audience: customers in other provinces, investors, partners and talent. Good coverage gives you something solid to share with all of them. You stay in control throughout, and nothing is published until you have approved the final text.</p><h2 id=\"who-pr-in-montreal-suits\">Who PR in Montreal suits</h2><p>We work with businesses in Montreal across very different fields. Technology and artificial intelligence start-ups use coverage to explain their work and attract hires. Fashion labels, designers and restaurants in the Plateau, Mile End and Old Montreal use it to reach customers who care about taste and originality. Life sciences firms, consultancies and professional practices use it to build trust with clients.</p><p>It particularly suits Montreal businesses that want to grow in English Canada. A strong English-language feature gives you a clear introduction to readers in Toronto, Ottawa and the West.</p><h2 id=\"the-montreal-media-landscape\">The Montreal media landscape</h2><p>Montreal is a bilingual media city. French-language papers such as La Presse and Le Devoir are central to public life in Quebec, while the <strong>Montreal Gazette</strong> is the city's long-standing English-language daily, covering business, politics, culture and community news. <strong>Cult Montreal</strong> focuses on arts, music, film, food and nightlife, which makes it a natural fit for creative and hospitality businesses.</p><p>The Gazette shares a newspaper family with the National Post, the Ottawa Citizen and the Calgary Herald, so a good Montreal story can travel. National titles such as Chatelaine and Toronto Life suit lifestyle and consumer angles aimed at readers elsewhere in Canada.</p><h2 id=\"what-stories-travel-in-montreal\">What stories travel in Montreal</h2><p>Montreal has a distinctive economy. It is a major centre for aerospace, home to companies such as Bombardier and CAE. It has one of the world's best-known video game industries, with large studios including Ubisoft Montreal, and a strong artificial intelligence research community around Mila and the city's universities, among them McGill and Concordia. Stories about innovation, research and skilled work land well here.</p><p>Culture travels too. The city hosts internationally known festivals such as Just for Laughs and the Montreal International Jazz Festival, and its food scene, from bagels to fine dining, draws visitors year round. Businesses that connect a genuine story to Montreal's creativity, its neighbourhoods or its European character tend to stand out.</p><h2 id=\"local-provincial-and-national-coverage\">Local, provincial and national coverage together</h2><p>A Montreal campaign often works best across several levels. A feature in the Montreal Gazette or Cult Montreal builds recognition at home. A related piece in the Ottawa Citizen or the Toronto Sun reaches neighbouring markets. A business angle in the Financial Post or the National Post introduces you to decision makers across Canada. We plan these together so each placement supports the others.</p><h2 id=\"how-it-works-with-dna\">How it works with DNA</h2><p>We start with your goals and the readers you want to reach. Then we:</p><ul><li><strong>Develop the story</strong>, finding the angle that suits each audience and outlet.</li><li><strong>Write it to the publication's standard</strong>, matching the tone of the Gazette, Cult Montreal or a national title.</li><li><strong>Manage the placement</strong> from first draft to publication.</li><li><strong>Ask for your approval</strong>, because you sign off every word before it goes live.</li></ul><p>Campaigns usually take weeks rather than days, and we keep you informed at each step.</p><h2 id=\"publications-we-place-in-montreal\">Publications we place in for Montreal</h2>\n<p>These are the Montreal titles we place clients in. Where a title has its own page, it explains what it publishes and how a feature there works.</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/get-featured-in/montreal-gazette\">Montreal Gazette</a></li><li><strong>Cult Montreal</strong></li></ul>\n<h3>Across Canada</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>Hello! Canada</strong></li><li><a href=\"/get-featured-in/national-post\">National Post</a></li><li><a href=\"/get-featured-in/toronto-sun\">Toronto Sun</a></li><li><a href=\"/get-featured-in/vancouver-sun\">Vancouver Sun</a></li><li><a href=\"/get-featured-in/financial-post\">Financial Post</a></li><li><a href=\"/get-featured-in/edmonton-journal\">Edmonton Journal</a></li><li><a href=\"/get-featured-in/calgary-herald\">Calgary Herald</a></li><li><strong>Toronto Life</strong></li><li><a href=\"/get-featured-in/ottawa-citizen\">Ottawa Citizen</a></li><li><a href=\"/get-featured-in/investing-com\">Investing.com</a></li><li><strong>Heywise</strong></li><li><strong>Chatelaine</strong></li><li><strong>Ottawa Sun</strong></li><li><strong>Today's Parent</strong></li><li><strong>Facty</strong></li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"frequently-asked-questions\">Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Do I need a PR agency based in Montreal?</h3><p>Not necessarily. What matters is knowing which titles suit your story and how to write for them. We work with Montreal businesses remotely, focusing on English-language coverage in the city and across Canada.</p><h3>How do I get featured in the Montreal Gazette?</h3><p>Start with a story that matters to Montreal readers, such as a local founder, a new venture or a fresh angle on technology, culture or food. We develop it, write it to the Gazette's standard and manage the placement, and you approve the final version.</p><h3>What does a Montreal PR agency do?</h3><p>It finds the newsworthy angle in your business, writes the article, places it with suitable local and national publications and makes sure the finished piece represents you accurately.</p>",
  "toc": [{"id": "who-pr-in-montreal-suits", "text": "Who PR in Montreal suits"}, {"id": "the-montreal-media-landscape", "text": "The Montreal media landscape"}, {"id": "what-stories-travel-in-montreal", "text": "What stories travel in Montreal"}, {"id": "local-provincial-and-national-coverage", "text": "Local, provincial and national coverage together"}, {"id": "how-it-works-with-dna", "text": "How it works with DNA"}, {"id": "publications-we-place-in-montreal", "text": "Publications we place in for Montreal"}, {"id": "frequently-asked-questions", "text": "Frequently asked questions"}],
  "takeaways": ["Montreal campaigns typically start with the Montreal Gazette and Cult Montreal, then extend to national titles such as the National Post and Financial Post.", "Aerospace, video games, artificial intelligence, festivals and food give Montreal businesses strong and distinctive story angles.", "DNA develops the story, writes it to each publication's standard and manages the placement, and you approve every word before it goes live."],
  "kind": "city",
  "area": "Montreal, Canada",
  "pubCount": 17
