  "body": "<p>A PR agency in Richmond helps your business appear in the publications that Virginia customers, partners and investors already read. It finds the part of your story that matters to people in central Virginia, writes it to the standard a newsroom expects and manages the process through to publication.</p><p>We work with businesses in Richmond remotely, including financial firms, law practices, health providers, food and drink brands and growing technology companies. We develop the story with you, write it to the publication's standard, manage the placement and give you a finished feature to share with clients and recruits. You approve every word before it goes live.</p><h2 id=\"who-pr-in-richmond-suits\">Who PR in Richmond suits</h2><p>As the state capital and a long-established commercial centre, Richmond has a business community that values reputation and relationships. PR tends to suit:</p><ul><li>Financial services and fintech firms working in a city with a strong banking and credit card presence</li><li>Law firms, consultancies and government contractors whose clients follow state business and policy news</li><li>Health and research organisations connected to the city's universities and hospitals</li><li>Restaurants, breweries and consumer brands in a city with a well-regarded food and drink scene</li><li>Founders who want to build a profile across Virginia, not just in one city</li></ul><h2 id=\"the-richmond-media-landscape\">The Richmond media landscape</h2><p>The <strong>Richmond Times-Dispatch</strong> is the city's main daily and the paper of record for central Virginia. Its business and local news coverage is read by owners, executives and civic leaders across the region, and a feature there carries real weight with Richmond customers.</p><p>Virginia also has a strong set of regional newspapers. Depending on where your customers are, a story can extend to <strong>The Virginian-Pilot</strong> and the <strong>Daily Press</strong> in Hampton Roads, <strong>The Roanoke Times</strong> in the south-west, <strong>The Daily Progress</strong> in Charlottesville or <strong>The Free Lance-Star</strong> in Fredericksburg. For readers who follow the state economy closely, <strong>Virginia Business</strong> is a natural fit. We tailor the angle to each title rather than sending one piece everywhere.</p><h2 id=\"what-stories-travel-in-richmond\">What stories travel in Richmond</h2><p>Richmond hosts the Federal Reserve Bank of Richmond and is home to companies such as Dominion Energy, Altria and CarMax, while Capital One runs large operations in the area. Virginia Commonwealth University and its health system are major employers, and the city has a growing reputation for food, craft beer and creative businesses. Stories that tend to land include:</p><ul><li>Finance, energy and consumer businesses with practical expertise to share</li><li>Health, research and university spin-outs with a Virginia connection</li><li>Independent food, drink and retail brands rooted in neighbourhoods such as Scott's Addition and Carytown</li><li>Firms responding to state policy, regulation and public sector demand</li><li>Founders who chose Richmond over Washington or larger East Coast cities</li></ul><p>Richmond readers are also interested in the city's history, its riverfront and how old industrial districts are being given new uses. A business with a real local story usually stands out more than one that only reports growth.</p><h2 id=\"local-state-and-national-coverage-together\">Local, state and national coverage together</h2><p>The most useful coverage usually works on three levels. A Richmond feature builds trust with nearby customers and partners. Virginia titles reach buyers in Norfolk, Roanoke, Charlottesville and Lynchburg, where many Richmond firms do a large share of their business. National coverage then gives you credibility with investors and customers who do not know the state. We plan the three together so your story is consistent and each piece strengthens the others.</p><h2 id=\"how-it-works-with-dna\">How it works with DNA</h2><p>We start by talking through your business, your customers and what you want coverage to do. We then shape the angle, draft the feature in the style of the target title and check the facts with you. You review the copy, ask for changes and approve the final version before anything is submitted. We manage the placement and send you the published feature.</p><p>Timings vary by publication, but you should expect weeks rather than days. We will tell you plainly which titles suit your story, and we never promise outcomes we do not control.</p><h2 id=\"publications-we-place-in-richmond\">Publications we place in for Richmond</h2>\n<p>These are the Richmond titles we place clients in. Where a title has its own page, it explains what it publishes and how a feature there works.</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/get-featured-in/richmond-times-dispatch\">Richmond Times-Dispatch</a></li></ul>\n<h3>Across Virginia</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>The Virginian-Pilot</strong></li><li><strong>Daily Press</strong></li><li><strong>The Roanoke Times</strong></li><li><strong>The Daily Progress</strong></li><li><strong>The News Leader</strong></li><li><strong>The News &amp; Advance</strong></li><li><strong>The Progress-Index</strong></li><li><strong>The Free Lance-Star</strong></li><li><strong>Martinsville Bulletin</strong></li><li><strong>Virginia Business</strong></li><li><strong>Bristol Herald Courier</strong></li><li><strong>Culpeper Star-Exponent</strong></li><li><strong>Danville Register &amp; Bee</strong></li><li><strong>The News Virginian</strong></li><li><strong>SWVA Today</strong></li></ul>\n<p>See every title we place in across the state on our <a href=\"/pr-in/virginia\">PR agency in Virginia</a> page.</p>\n<h2 id=\"frequently-asked-questions\">Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Do I need a PR agency based in Richmond?</h3><p>No. You need an agency that understands Richmond readers and the Virginia titles your customers follow. We work with Richmond businesses remotely and keep you involved at every step through calls, drafts and approvals.</p><h3>How do I get featured in the Richmond Times-Dispatch?</h3><p>Begin with a story that is clearly relevant to central Virginia readers, such as a local expansion, a new service or a founder with a strong view on their sector. We help you find that angle, write it to the paper's standard and manage the placement.</p><h3>What does a Richmond PR agency do?</h3><p>It helps you decide what to say, writes it in a form that publications will accept and places it in front of the readers you care about. For Richmond firms that usually means local coverage first, with Virginia regional and national titles added where they suit the story.</p>",
