  "title": "PR Agency in San Jose: Get Featured in Local Media",
  "description": "A PR agency for San Jose and Silicon Valley businesses. We shape your story and place it in the Mercury News and wider California media you approve.",
  "intro": "San Jose sits at the heart of Silicon Valley, yet many of its companies struggle to explain what they do to anyone outside the industry. A PR agency in San Jose helps you tell that story clearly to local readers, buyers and future hires.",
  "outlets": ["hollywood-life", "hollywood-reporter", "la-weekly", "oc-register", "san-diego-union-tribune"],
  "body": "<p>A PR agency in San Jose takes the work your company is doing and turns it into a story that Silicon Valley readers will understand and remember. For engineering-led companies, that often means translating technical progress into something that matters to customers, investors and the community around them.</p><p>For San Jose businesses, Digital Networking Agency develops the story with you, writes it to the publication's standard, manages the placement and asks you to approve every word before it goes live. The coverage then works hard for you in sales conversations, recruitment and investor updates.</p><h2 id=\"who-pr-in-san-jose-suits\">Who PR in San Jose suits</h2><p>We work with businesses in San Jose across technology and beyond it.</p><ul><li><strong>Technology companies</strong> in semiconductors, hardware, networking and enterprise software that want to be understood outside their niche.</li><li><strong>Founders and engineers</strong> building a public profile in a region where reputation opens doors.</li><li><strong>Family-owned and community businesses</strong> serving San Jose's Vietnamese, Mexican American, Indian American and other communities.</li><li><strong>Property, healthcare and professional firms</strong> that serve a growing South Bay population.</li></ul><h2 id=\"the-san-jose-media-landscape\">The San Jose media landscape</h2><p>The Mercury News is San Jose's daily newspaper and has covered Silicon Valley since long before the name was common. Its readers include engineers, executives and long-time residents, and its pages combine technology and business reporting with local news about housing, transport and city life. That breadth means a well-chosen story can reach both the industry and the wider community.</p><p>Business Journal Silicon Valley is another important title for company news, with a readership of owners, executives and investors across the South Bay and Peninsula. Deciding whether your story belongs in a daily newspaper or a business-focused title is one of the first choices we make together.</p><h2 id=\"what-stories-travel-in-san-jose\">What stories travel in San Jose</h2><p>San Jose's economy is built on technology, but the stories that travel are rarely about specifications alone. Readers respond to people, place and consequence.</p><ul><li><strong>Technology with a human angle</strong>, such as a product built in the South Bay that changes how people work or live.</li><li><strong>Founder and immigrant journeys</strong>, which reflect how many of the region's companies were actually started.</li><li><strong>Manufacturing and supply chain</strong>, including companies that still design and build physical products in the valley.</li><li><strong>Community and downtown life</strong>, from new restaurants to businesses investing in the city centre.</li></ul><h2 id=\"local-state-and-national-coverage-together\">Local, state and national coverage together</h2><p>San Jose companies often sell nationally or globally, so local coverage is usually one part of a wider plan. A story in the Mercury News can sit alongside coverage in the East Bay Times for readers across the bay, or in statewide titles such as the LA Times, The Sacramento Bee or the San Diego Union Tribune. Consumer and lifestyle brands may also suit LA Magazine or Flaunt Magazine. We plan the combination around where your customers, partners and future employees actually spend their time.</p><h2 id=\"how-it-works-with-dna\">How it works with DNA</h2><p>We work with San Jose businesses remotely, which fits the way most Silicon Valley teams already operate. The process has three steps.</p><ul><li><strong>Story development:</strong> we learn what you do and agree an angle that a San Jose reader will care about.</li><li><strong>Writing:</strong> we write the piece to the standard and style of the chosen publication.</li><li><strong>Placement:</strong> we manage the placement, and you approve every word before it goes live.</li></ul><p>Most placements come together over weeks rather than days, depending on the title and the story.</p><h2 id=\"publications-we-place-in-san-jose\">Publications we place in for San Jose</h2>\n<p>These are the San Jose titles we place clients in. Where a title has its own page, it explains what it publishes and how a feature there works.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Mercury News</strong></li></ul>\n<h3>Across California</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>LA Times</strong></li><li><a href=\"/get-featured-in/hollywood-reporter\">The Hollywood Reporter</a></li><li><strong>Business Journal Silicon Valley</strong></li><li><a href=\"/get-featured-in/oc-register\">OC Register</a></li><li><a href=\"/get-featured-in/san-diego-union-tribune\">San Diego Union Tribune</a></li><li><strong>The Sacramento Bee</strong></li><li><strong>Flaunt Magazine</strong></li><li><a href=\"/get-featured-in/hollywood-life\">Hollywood Life</a></li><li><strong>East Bay Times</strong></li><li><strong>LA Magazine</strong></li><li><strong>The Fresno Bee</strong></li><li><a href=\"/get-featured-in/la-weekly\">LA Weekly</a></li><li><strong>VC Star</strong></li><li><strong>The Desert Sun</strong></li><li><strong>San Luis Obispo Tribune</strong></li></ul>\n<p>See every title we place in across the state on our <a href=\"/pr-in/california\">PR agency in California</a> page.</p>\n<h2 id=\"frequently-asked-questions\">Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Do I need a PR agency based in San Jose?</h3><p>No. What you need is an agency that understands Silicon Valley media and its readers. We work with San Jose businesses remotely and plan each story around the titles your audience already reads.</p><h3>How do I get featured in the Mercury News?</h3><p>Bring a story with a clear San Jose or Silicon Valley connection and explain why it matters now. We develop the angle with you, write it to the paper's standard and manage the placement, with your approval on the final wording.</p><h3>What does a San Jose PR agency do?</h3><p>It helps local companies explain their work in plain terms and places that story in the media Silicon Valley reads. With DNA, that covers story development, writing and placement, and you sign off every word.</p>",
  "toc": [{"id": "who-pr-in-san-jose-suits", "text": "Who PR in San Jose suits"}, {"id": "the-san-jose-media-landscape", "text": "The San Jose media landscape"}, {"id": "what-stories-travel-in-san-jose", "text": "What stories travel in San Jose"}, {"id": "local-state-and-national-coverage-together", "text": "Local, state and national coverage together"}, {"id": "how-it-works-with-dna", "text": "How it works with DNA"}, {"id": "publications-we-place-in-san-jose", "text": "Publications we place in for San Jose"}, {"id": "frequently-asked-questions", "text": "Frequently asked questions"}],
