  "slug": "south-africa",
  "region": "South Africa",
  "h1": "PR Agency in South Africa",
  "title": "PR Agency in South Africa: Get Featured in SA Media",
  "description": "A PR agency for South Africa: we develop your story and place it in business, lifestyle and culture media read across the country, with your approval first.",
  "intro": "We work with businesses in South Africa, and with international companies entering the market, to win coverage in the business, lifestyle and culture titles South Africans read.",
  "outlets": ["investing-com"],
  "body": "<p>A PR agency in South Africa helps your business appear in the publications South Africans trust, and in the search results that follow. The country's media is concentrated in Johannesburg and Cape Town but read nationally, with strong business titles, lifestyle magazines and digital news brands that reach audiences at home and in the South African diaspora.</p><p>DNA works with businesses in South Africa remotely. We find the story in what you do, write it to the standard of the publication it is going to, manage the placement and keep you in control. You approve every word before anything goes live. The articles that result support conversations with investors, partners and customers, and give anyone looking you up something credible to find.</p><h2 id=\"who-pr-in-south-africa-suits\">Who PR in South Africa suits</h2><p>We work with a range of South African businesses and individuals, most often:</p><ul><li><strong>Founders and fintech companies</strong> in Johannesburg and Cape Town building credibility with investors.</li><li><strong>Luxury, fashion and lifestyle brands</strong> that want to be seen by discerning consumers.</li><li><strong>Hospitality, wine and tourism businesses</strong> in the Western Cape and other destinations.</li><li><strong>Interior design, architecture and property firms</strong> with work worth showing.</li><li><strong>International companies</strong> entering South Africa or using it as a base for the wider continent.</li></ul><h2 id=\"the-south-africa-media-landscape\">The South Africa media landscape</h2><p>South Africa has a well-developed press. Business Day, the Financial Mail, the Mail &amp; Guardian and the Daily Maverick are among the best-known names for news and analysis. For business coverage aimed at founders and executives, Business Insider Africa and Fast Company Africa give South African companies a voice that also reaches readers elsewhere on the continent. The South African is a digital news brand read widely at home and by South Africans abroad.</p><p>Lifestyle coverage is strong. GQ South Africa and Glamour South Africa reach style-conscious readers, House &amp; Garden Africa covers interiors and design, and the Robb Report speaks to an audience interested in luxury. Billboard and Time give music and profile stories an international dimension. Titles such as I Love South Africa and SA Promo focus on local pride, travel and things to do, which suits hospitality and consumer brands.</p><h2 id=\"what-stories-travel-in-south-africa\">What stories travel in South Africa</h2><p>Johannesburg is the country's financial and commercial centre, home to the Johannesburg Stock Exchange and the headquarters of many large companies, so stories about growth, leadership and investment fit there. Cape Town has become known for technology start-ups, creative industries and tourism, and the nearby Winelands give wine and food stories a natural setting. Durban's port makes trade and logistics a strong theme.</p><p>Mining remains part of the national story, and the Eastern Cape has an established automotive manufacturing base. Fintech, renewable energy and entrepreneurship are frequent subjects, as are stories about job creation and skills, which matter to readers across the country. South African audiences appreciate stories that are grounded in local reality, so a piece that explains what you do for South African customers will land better than one written for another market.</p><h2 id=\"local-national-and-international-coverage-together\">Local, national and international coverage together</h2><p>We usually plan South African coverage in layers. A feature in a lifestyle or local-interest title reaches the consumers who can act on it. A business placement shows partners and investors that you are an established company. Pan-African and international titles then extend your reach beyond South Africa. Together they give anyone searching your name a consistent picture.</p><h2 id=\"how-it-works-with-dna\">How it works with DNA</h2><p>We start by understanding your business, your customers and your goals. We recommend the titles that fit, develop the angle and write the article to that publication's style. You review the draft, request changes and approve the final version. We then manage the placement and send you the live article. Expect the process to take weeks rather than days.</p><h2 id=\"publications-we-place-in-south-africa\">Publications we place in across South Africa</h2>\n<p>A selection of the titles we place clients in. Where a title has its own page, it explains what it publishes and how a feature there works.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Business Insider Africa</strong></li><li><strong>The South African</strong></li><li><a href=\"/get-featured-in/investing-com\">Investing.com</a></li><li><strong>GQ South Africa</strong></li><li><strong>House &amp; Garden Africa</strong></li><li><strong>Time.com</strong></li><li><strong>Women Stuff</strong></li><li><strong>I Love South Africa</strong></li><li><strong>Men Stuff</strong></li><li><strong>Fast Company Africa</strong></li><li><strong>Billboard</strong></li><li><strong>Robb Report</strong></li><li><strong>SA Promo</strong></li><li><strong>Glamour South Africa</strong></li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"frequently-asked-questions\">Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Do I need a PR agency based in South Africa?</h3><p>No. What matters is knowing which South African publications reach your audience and how they write. We work with businesses in South Africa remotely, from Johannesburg and Cape Town to Durban and beyond.</p><h3>How do I get featured in South African media?</h3><p>Begin with a story that matters to South African readers, such as local jobs, a new product, a founder journey or expert insight. We develop it, write it to the publication's standard and manage the placement after your approval.</p><h3>Can an international brand get coverage in South Africa?</h3><p>Yes. Stories about entering the South African market, partnering with local businesses or serving South African customers are a common and effective starting point.</p>",
  "toc": [{"id": "who-pr-in-south-africa-suits", "text": "Who PR in South Africa suits"}, {"id": "the-south-africa-media-landscape", "text": "The South Africa media landscape"}, {"id": "what-stories-travel-in-south-africa", "text": "What stories travel in South Africa"}, {"id": "local-national-and-international-coverage-together", "text": "Local, national and international coverage together"}, {"id": "how-it-works-with-dna", "text": "How it works with DNA"}, {"id": "publications-we-place-in-south-africa", "text": "Publications we place in across South Africa"}, {"id": "frequently-asked-questions", "text": "Frequently asked questions"}],
  "takeaways": ["South African coverage spans business titles, lifestyle magazines and digital news brands, each reaching a different audience in Johannesburg, Cape Town, Durban and beyond.", "Stories tied to finance, fintech, mining, wine, tourism, design and entrepreneurship fit the way South African media covers the country.", "DNA develops the story, writes it to each publication's standard and manages placement, and you approve every word before it goes live."],
  "kind": "country",
