  "slug": "tulsa",
  "region": "Tulsa",
  "h1": "PR Agency in Tulsa",
  "title": "PR Agency in Tulsa: Get Featured in Oklahoma Media",
  "description": "A PR agency in Tulsa that turns your work into features in the Tulsa World and Oklahoma titles, written to each publication's standard and approved by you.",
  "intro": "Digital Networking Agency helps Tulsa businesses get featured in the Tulsa World and in titles across Oklahoma. We develop the story, write it to the publication's standard and manage the placement, and you approve every word.",
  "outlets": ["tulsa-world"],
  "body": "<p>A PR agency in Tulsa helps your business appear in the publications that Oklahoma customers, partners and investors already read. It identifies the story in your work that will matter to people in Tulsa and across the state, writes it to the standard a newsroom expects and manages the process until it is published.</p><p>We work with businesses in Tulsa remotely, from energy and aerospace firms to start-ups, health providers, hospitality businesses and professional services. We develop the story with you, write it to the publication's standard, manage the placement and give you a finished feature to use with clients and recruits. You approve every word before it goes live.</p><h2 id=\"who-pr-in-tulsa-suits\">Who PR in Tulsa suits</h2><p>Tulsa is a city that is actively reinventing itself, and its business community pays attention to companies that are part of that change. PR tends to suit:</p><ul><li>Energy companies and their suppliers, especially those working on new technologies and transition projects</li><li>Aerospace, manufacturing and engineering businesses serving customers across the region</li><li>Start-ups and remote-first founders who have chosen Tulsa as their base</li><li>Health, education and non-profit organisations with a strong community story</li><li>Restaurants, venues and creative businesses in the city's revived districts</li></ul><h2 id=\"the-tulsa-media-landscape\">The Tulsa media landscape</h2><p>The <strong>Tulsa World</strong> is the city's main daily and the title most people in north-eastern Oklahoma turn to for local news, business and sport. A feature there gives a Tulsa company credibility with customers who read it regularly and with the civic leaders who follow the city's development closely.</p><p>Beyond Tulsa, a story can reach readers in Oklahoma City and across the state through <strong>The Oklahoman</strong>, while <strong>The Journal Record</strong> is read by people who follow Oklahoma business, law and policy in detail. Closer to home, the <strong>Examiner-Enterprise</strong> serves Bartlesville and the surrounding area. We tailor the angle to each title rather than sending the same piece everywhere.</p><h2 id=\"what-stories-travel-in-tulsa\">What stories travel in Tulsa</h2><p>Tulsa was once known as the Oil Capital of the World, and energy still shapes its economy, with companies such as Williams and ONEOK at home in the city. Aerospace is another pillar, including a large airline maintenance base. In recent years Tulsa has drawn attention for attracting remote workers, for the Gathering Place park and for its Art Deco architecture, while the history of the Greenwood District has become an important part of how the city tells its own story. Stories that tend to travel include:</p><ul><li>Energy and engineering firms with practical insight into a changing industry</li><li>Aerospace and advanced manufacturing businesses growing in the region</li><li>Founders and remote workers who moved to Tulsa and built something here</li><li>Businesses investing in the Tulsa Arts District, the Blue Dome District, Cherry Street or Brookside</li><li>Organisations contributing to Greenwood and to community renewal across the city</li></ul><h2 id=\"local-state-and-national-coverage-together\">Local, state and national coverage together</h2><p>The most useful coverage works on three levels. A Tulsa feature builds trust with nearby customers and partners. Oklahoma titles extend that reach to Oklahoma City and smaller towns where many Tulsa firms do a large share of their business. National coverage gives you credibility with investors and customers who know Tulsa only by reputation. We plan the three together so your story is consistent and each piece supports the others.</p><h2 id=\"how-it-works-with-dna\">How it works with DNA</h2><p>We begin with a conversation about your business, your audience and what you want coverage to achieve. We then shape the angle, draft the feature in the style of the target publication and check the facts with you. You review the draft, request any changes and approve the final copy before anything is submitted. We manage the placement and send you the published feature.</p><p>Timings vary by title, but you should expect weeks rather than days. We will tell you plainly which publications suit your story, and we never promise outcomes we cannot control.</p><h2 id=\"publications-we-place-in-tulsa\">Publications we place in for Tulsa</h2>\n<p>These are the Tulsa titles we place clients in. Where a title has its own page, it explains what it publishes and how a feature there works.</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/get-featured-in/tulsa-world\">Tulsa World</a></li></ul>\n<h3>Across Oklahoma</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>The Oklahoman</strong></li><li><strong>The Journal Record</strong></li><li><strong>Examiner-Enterprise</strong></li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"frequently-asked-questions\">Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Do I need a PR agency based in Tulsa?</h3><p>No. What matters is an agency that understands Tulsa readers and the Oklahoma titles your customers follow. We work with Tulsa businesses remotely and keep you involved through calls, drafts and approvals.</p><h3>How do I get featured in the Tulsa World?</h3><p>Start with a story that is clearly relevant to Tulsa readers, such as a local expansion, a new service or a founder with a strong view of their industry. We help you develop that angle, write it to the paper's standard and manage the placement.</p><h3>What does a Tulsa PR agency do?</h3><p>It helps you work out what to say, writes it in a form publications will accept and places it in front of the readers who matter to you. For Tulsa firms that usually means city coverage first, with Oklahoma and national titles where they suit the story.</p>",
  "toc": [{"id": "who-pr-in-tulsa-suits", "text": "Who PR in Tulsa suits"}, {"id": "the-tulsa-media-landscape", "text": "The Tulsa media landscape"}, {"id": "what-stories-travel-in-tulsa", "text": "What stories travel in Tulsa"}, {"id": "local-state-and-national-coverage-together", "text": "Local, state and national coverage together"}, {"id": "how-it-works-with-dna", "text": "How it works with DNA"}, {"id": "publications-we-place-in-tulsa", "text": "Publications we place in for Tulsa"}, {"id": "frequently-asked-questions", "text": "Frequently asked questions"}],
  "takeaways": ["A Tulsa PR agency turns your work into published features that Oklahoma customers, partners and investors will read.", "The Tulsa World leads locally, with The Oklahoman and The Journal Record extending reach across the state.", "Energy, aerospace, remote-first founders and the city's cultural renewal are the themes that carry Tulsa stories."],
  "kind": "city",
